  "description": "JUSSAU crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H84 Er4 N12 O16 S6,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er1B (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2B (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.498-3.813 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.07-112.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er4(acac)4(L)6(μ3-OH)2]·2CH3CN (paper EA C108H90Er4N13O17S6; CCDC C104H84Er4N12O16S6·2(C2H3N)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
